    "problem_statement": "Ok.unwrap() returns incorrect value\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `unwrap()` method on `Ok` instances is returning an incorrect value. When calling `unwrap()` on an `Ok` result, it returns the wrapped value plus 1 instead of the actual wrapped value.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom result import Ok\n\n# Create an Ok result with a string value\nok_result = Ok('yay')\nprint(f\"Expected: 'yay', Got: {ok_result.unwrap()}\")\n\n# Create an Ok result with an integer value  \nok_int = Ok(123)\nprint(f\"Expected: 123, Got: {ok_int.unwrap()}\")\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\nExpected: 'yay', Got: yay\nExpected: 123, Got: 123\n```\n\nActual output:\n```\nExpected: 'yay', Got: TypeError: can only concatenate str (not \"int\") to str\nExpected: 123, Got: 124\n```\n\nThe method appears to be adding 1 to the wrapped value, which causes type errors for non-numeric types and incorrect values for numeric types."
